# SP-OKF (G-OKF-CONFORM) ignore list for the public Position_Is_Arithmetic repo.
# One glob per line, matched against the bundle-relative path OR the basename. '#' = comment.
# Spec: shannon-prime-lattice/papers/SP-OKF-PROFILE.md §4.
#
# The live, public-facing knowledge bundles ARE validated:
#   papers/           (paper-bite + gate-receipt)
#   research papers/  (research-paper + paper-provenance)   <- the Phase-0 pilot
#   posts/            (log: field notes / updates)
#
# Ignored below = NOT live knowledge concepts:

# Top-level repo-meta / navigation docs (plain markdown by convention, like a README).
# NOTE: the validator matches each glob against BOTH the bundle-relative path and the basename,
# so a bare `README.md` here would also (wrongly) ignore the per-paper companion `papers/*/README.md`
# bites, which ARE knowledge concepts and carry frontmatter. We therefore path-anchor the root
# README with a leading-segment glob that cannot match a nested basename. AGENTS/HISTORY/LEDGER/
# SERIES/etc. have basenames unique to the repo root, so listing them bare is safe.
/README.md
AGENTS.md
HISTORY.md
LEDGER.md
SERIES.md
METHODOLOGY.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
COMPANION-THEORY.md
GEMMA4-QUANT-FIX.md

# Archived/ = superseded historical docs (an archive, not the live bundle). Some carry legacy
# frontmatter, most are pre-SP-OKF; not in scope for conformance.
Archived/*
Archived/**
